+# Editorial direction
+
+## 2026-07-12
+
+**Thesis.** In this frozen small model, matched clause retrieval is governed more clearly by answer position and lexical competition than by context amount: end placement helps, naive word-overlap pruning strengthens the decoy, and removing that retained decoy reverses the failure, while the measured length effect is unresolved.
+
+**Significance.** The result informs builders of offline small-model document QA deciding whether to shorten prompts with lexical filters: a cheap filter needs a decoy-resistant comparison before deployment, and the observed end-position gain is diagnostic rather than an automatic remedy.
+
+**Originality.** Unlike NoLiMa's demonstration that literal overlap makes long-context tests too easy, this study uses paired synthetic clauses on a frozen laptop-scale open model to show that the same overlap can make keyword pruning select a competing answer and to diagnose the failure by removing only that competitor.
+
+I replaced the stale completed focus item with a full-lap demand for a second deployable selector baseline, then directed a paper-wide reframe and a defensible descriptive treatment of uncertainty. These moves answer the review's significance, originality, and soundness objections in that order. Readability work should leave only displays that change the argument, put denominators beside position estimates, and replace repeated bold mini-headlines and signed-direction wording with direct claim-evidence prose.
+
+The quality-code-density complaint has persisted since iter 3 and is terminally **unfixable in this environment**. The current filler contrast changes topic, domain, entity and code density, candidate count, and templates together; no post hoc analysis can isolate relevance, while a sufficiently matched factorial rerun cannot fit the locked laptop clean-room budget alongside the required grid. Writers must own this in Limitations, remove quality from the contribution and answered questions, and call the result only a comparison of the two generated filler bundles. The practical end-placement recommendation and the one-sentence competitor shift are also unfixable from paid outputs: present them as diagnostic limitations and narrow all claims accordingly.
+
+Done means a later review marks the selector-baseline complaint resolved; the manuscript leads with the position-and-decoy thesis; uncertainty is explicitly descriptive at the family level; the confounded quality comparison is secondary or omitted; and every remaining display is readable, denominator-complete, and necessary to the argument.
